message: "If you use this archive, please cite the article below. A Zenodo DOI for the archive itself can be added under 'identifiers' once minted."
title: "Reproducibility archive for: When Logical Staleness Attracts - Training-stage and Assignment-dependent Selection Geometry of Multi-Krum under Non-IID Federated Learning"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jiang"
    given-names: "Lu"
    affiliation: "School of Electronic and Optical Engineering, Nanjing University of Science and Technology, Nanjing, Jiangsu 210094, China"
repository-code: "https://github.com/<USER>/<REPO>"
url: "https://github.com/<USER>/<REPO>"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - federated learning
  - Byzantine-robust aggregation
  - Multi-Krum
  - non-IID data
  - logical staleness
  - selection geometry
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Audited processed evidence and analysis code for a controlled study of how
  logical staleness and resource assignment shape honest-client selection under
  Multi-Krum. The archive contains the resolved configurations, processed tables,
  integrity ledgers, verification programs and figure-generation code for the
  reported 15 Stage 8, 18 Stage 9 and 27 Stage 10 runs. Raw smoke, partial and
  cached logs are excluded; project and user paths were replaced by portable
  placeholders during de-identification. Original code is MIT licensed, original
  data and documentation are CC BY 4.0, and the modified third-party files under
  vendor/FLPoison remain GPL-2.0 as described in LICENSING.md.
